        <td>Incline push-ups</td>
        <td>30 seconds</td>
        <td>Use wall if needed</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Squat to chair</td>
        <td>30 seconds</td>
        <td>Sit and stand</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Glute bridges</td>
        <td>30 seconds</td>
        <td>Hold at top</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Knee plank</td>
        <td>20 seconds</td>
        <td>Build to 30</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Marching in place</td>
        <td>30 seconds</td>
        <td>Warm-up/cooldown</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p class="text-mute">Perform this circuit 2-3 times, resting 60 seconds between sets. Total time: 10-15 minutes.</p>

  <h2>Progression Timeline</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Weeks 1-2:</strong> Master form with modifications, 2 sessions per week</li>
    <li><strong>Weeks 3-4:</strong> Increase hold times by 10-15 seconds</li>
    <li><strong>Weeks 5-6:</strong> Add one additional circuit round</li>
    <li><strong>Weeks 7-8:</strong> Transition from modified to standard versions</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Safety Guidelines</h2>
  <p>Stop immediately if you feel sharp pain, dizziness, or shortness of breath. Consult a healthcare provider before starting any new exercise program.</p>
  <p>For proper form review, consult our <a href="/workouts/home-workouts/">home workouts guide</a> or use video resources showing each movement.</p>

  <h2>Nutrition for Beginners</h2>
  <p>Your body needs adequate protein and energy to adapt to training. Use our <a href="/protein-calculator/">protein calculator</a> to determine your daily target. Pair workouts with proper hydration and post-exercise nutrition for optimal recovery.</p>

